  "term": "Millon Clinical Multiaxial Inventory",
  "definition": "The Millon Clinical Multiaxial Inventory is a psychological assessment that uses true/false questions. It is used with adults as a screening or clinical evaluation tool when they have emotional or interpersonal difficulties or are being assessed during psychotherapy or a psychodiagnostic evaluation.",
